Ladybird builds the area a float excludes content from out of its
margin box, negative margins included, and clamps only a negative
height to zero, leaving an empty area at its margin box’s top edge.
Blink’s CreateExclusionArea() in floats_utils.cc adds the block-axis
margins to the fragment’s block size and clamps the sum at zero.
Gecko’s nsFloatManager::CalculateRegionFor() inflates the float’s rect
by its margins and sets a negative block size to zero. And WebKit’s
RenderBlockFlow::positionNewFloats() gives the float object the height
of its box plus its before and after margins, and a float object with
a negative height intersects no line.
